    "body": "Line: unified geometric integration · count2/3 · headline dev437/512 plus opened0/128 -> unchanged (panel fitting; fresh acceptance unmet).\n\nReferences #2030. Named run: unified-geometric-carrier-437-20261011. ONE combined interrupted-result/audit delivery, following merged preparation #2210. No runtime source, panel, grader, criterion or model default changes.\n\n## Result\n\n- Source5f835ac51, actual CUDA binary31fca86a. Three independent exact saved437 baselines, original-eight parity, export/master/frozen reloads and full512 seals pass. Fixed128-update endpoints OFF1001/ON1001/OFF2001 each score0/512. No candidate replaces saved437.\n- Owner stopped ON2001 during its partial baseline, before optimizer. UNFINISHED_NOT_NEGATIVE; no false completed seal. Four-arm contrast incomplete; opened128 and genuinely fresh qualification NOT_RUN; no mechanism closure.\n- All outputs/builds/partial receipts have verified cloud custody; owned4090 was released/deleted. Official down ledger13,412s at$0.89/h estimates$3.315744 for this pod, not the entire cycle.\n\n## Audit And Changed Next Action\n\n- Independently reconstructed512/512 labels and actual target bytes from raw query/source records; no contradictory identical inputs or token/output-budget obstruction. All6664 saved canonical positions have positive target mass.\n- The panel is128 supplied banks,48 answers,12 queries, two records per row, current job/residence only. It is a literal-emitter component instrument, not predicted compiler/store/conversation or full-geometry/energy acceptance.\n- Source establishes changing Context/prototypes under frozen learned factors, mixed full120/ambient4 credit and an existing Prefix finite-utility option explicitly disabled. These are unresolved integration risks, not proven collapse causes. Seed2001OFF has no correct canonical first token and only14 EOS; its zero is not solely an EOS/whitespace rejection.\n- Actual current SpiralCore browser text routes, labelled E8 inverse replay and a small Bell PCM frame round trip observed; source hash recorded. Claude's delivered E8 memory already imports SpiralCore's group. Latest Starling pivot, exact icosian norm/device work and newly merged2218 activation result credited. Retracted2212 kernel speed claim excluded.\n- Next changes the coherent typed binding/frame/native-credit connection before any new preregistration/FIT. No old-recipe resume, opened diagnostic, new model compute, rate/dose/seed sweep or criterion changes.\n- Opposite outcome: contradictory/unproducible labels require an authoring/panel blocker and owner direction; useful replicated candidates proceed to fixed diagnostic then genuine fresh qualification. Current coherent panel plus collapsed configurations instead requires a model-path repair. No architecture-wide negative follows.\n\n## Exact-Head Validation / Review\n\nFinal head6029d5025adc10571d0c7748779b94b43c9800ef: git diff --check origin/main...HEAD PASS; existing claim-wording gate PASS. Documentation only: no Rust compile, fixture rerun or model execution in this delivery. Static existing-input audit and source/receipt review are separately scoped. Earlier source/CUDA checks belong to5f835ac51, not this documentation head. Compatibility acknowledgements are not tests. Claude2218's main entry and STATUS/ROADMAP edits are preserved. An ancestry-only merge retains our earlier transport commit without rewriting remote history; final document tree is the reviewed updated tree.\n\nExact-head self-review: checked source/data identities, three complete versus one unsealed/never-optimized arm, field/active/frozen inventories, compiler/store bypass, grader limitations, geometry-domain separation, newest Claude2218 receipts, preserved peer entries, retracted DeepSeek kernel, cloud/pod receipts, and unchanged acceptance. No blocking documentation findings. Native collapse cause and entire serving/energy path remain unqualified.\n\n## Inclusive Cost\n\nSame cycle from2026-10-10T21:28UTC, no reset. One immutable conservative97,320,000ms charge envelope through2026-10-12T00:30UTC includes numerical preparation/failures/replacements, builds, all model work, waits, cloud, interruption, audit, review and protected delivery/cleanup. Prior1,522,332,185ms plus charge -> effective1,619,652,185ms against1,650,772,756ms. Excess tail is added without double counting. Native ledger rebuild in an owned copy rejects an unmapped historical receipt; real prior view was not reset. Explicit charge/carry receipt retained, no false native accounting PASS; historical mapping must resolve before new model admission.\n\nCanonical record, whole-path audit, newest-first state, mechanism, README, STATUS and ROADMAP updated together. Continue protected merge/fresh-main tree verification and delete the temporary branch/worktree after verified custody. This ends the interrupted cycle, never the continuous research goal.\n",
